d says hey babe i should be back in  one or two days obviously hawkeye is not  going to leave kate bishop just to die  because as it's very clear here the  tracksuit mafia is still after now both  of them hawkeye's reflexes are still  just as good as before as one of the  members of the tracksuit mafia throws a  molotov cocktail at the window in which  hawkeye and kate bishop are in the  building he quickly breaks the window  catches the bottle throws it back at him  and lights them on fire their tracksuits  and all and from here we see that  hawkeye's not exactly having the best  time trying to get rid of this mafia off  his back he's got several bruises on his  body so does kate bishop he's ziplining  and it breaks but as you can see there's  another zip line down below which he's  probably going to catch hawkeye says  things have gotten a little more  complicated and we can see him put a lot  of ice packs all over his body clearly  taking care of kate and dealing with the  tracksuit mafia has proven a little bit  harder than he thought it would be he's  getting beat up he's getting shot at and  he's getting kidnapped but don't worry  kate bishop is quickly coming to the  rescue sort  of now from here we see a lot of quick  action sequences but one thing that's  very important to note here is we see  vera farmiga's character eleanor bishop  the mother of kate bishop now in the  comics it was believed that eleanor  bishop died when kate was very very  young however later on it was actually  revealed that she was alive and  directing the activities of kate's  nemesis in the comics madame mask madam  mask has caused lots of trouble for tony  stark shield and others over time and  she's also cloned herself several times  as well and it looks like eleanor and  madam mask could be the true villains  behind everything that we're seeing in  the hawkeye series because the tracksuit  mafia is cool but there's got to be a  bigger villain than them and since they  showed elea